---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import PageCTA from '../components/PageCTA.astro';
import TermSwap from '../components/TermSwap.astro';

const title = 'Forge - code intelligence · metalmind';
const description = 'Cross-repo code graph with HTTP-route edges, symbol-aware navigation, and coordinated rename through Serena\'s LSP backend.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHero
    metal="bronze"
    eyebrow="graph"
    eyebrowScadrial="burn bronze"
    title="Sight across repos, not just one."
    sub="Forge is metalmind's cross-repo code graph. HTTP-route edges connect a caller in service A to its handler in service B - across language, framework, and repo boundaries - with provenance Claude can trust-grade."
  />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="feat-grid">
        <div class="feat-card">
          <div class="feat-num mono accent-text">01</div>
          <h3 class="display feat-h">Three edge tiers</h3>
          <p>OpenAPI specs on the metalmind shelf (never inside your repos), Java RestTemplate / WebClient / Feign callers, and URL string literals as an opt-in fallback. Each edge carries <span class="kbd">INFERRED_NAME</span>, <span class="kbd">INFERRED_ROUTE</span>, and <span class="kbd">INFERRED_URL_LITERAL</span> provenance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feat-card">
          <div class="feat-num mono accent-text">02</div>
          <h3 class="display feat-h">Symbol-aware navigation</h3>
          <p>
            <TermSwap classic="symbol" scadrial="burn iron" mono />
            returns a symbol's neighbors - who calls it, what it calls, its module.
            <TermSwap classic="rename" scadrial="burn steel" mono />
            drives a coordinated rename through Serena's LSP backend, across every repo in the forge.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feat-card">
          <div class="feat-num mono accent-text">03</div>
          <h3 class="display feat-h">Team-debug, primed</h3>
          <p>
            <TermSwap classic="debug" scadrial="burn zinc" mono />
            hands a bug to the <span class="kbd">/team-debug</span> skill with the code graph already loaded. The team agents start with context, not cold.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">§ Walkthrough</div>
        <h2>One query. Two repos. One answer.</h2>
        <p>A caller in <span class="kbd">billing-svc</span>; a handler in <span class="kbd">notif-svc</span>. Native Claude has no concept of "the other service's code." Forge does.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="term forge-term">
        <div class="term-bar">
          <div class="term-dot"></div><div class="term-dot"></div><div class="term-dot"></div>
          <div class="term-title mono">forge - graph query</div>
        </div>
        <div class="term-body">
          <div><span class="meta"># add each repo to the forge group, one per call</span></div>
          <div><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">metalmind forge add</span> <span class="arg">payments ~/repos/billing-svc</span></div>
          <div><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">metalmind forge add</span> <span class="arg">payments ~/repos/notif-svc</span></div>
          <div><span class="ok">✓</span> <span class="meta">2 repos · indexed in 6.2s</span></div>
          <div>&nbsp;</div>
          <div><span class="meta"># query across both</span></div>
          <div>
            <span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">metalmind <TermSwap classic="graph" scadrial="burn bronze" /></span> <span class="arg">"how does payment-failed reach the user?"</span> <span class="meta"><TermSwap classic="--group" scadrial="--forge" /> payments</span>
          </div>
          <div>&nbsp;</div>
          <div><span class="hl">→ billing-svc/src/handlers/charge.ts:142</span></div>
          <div>  <span class="meta">notifyClient.post('/notifications/payment-failed', ...)</span></div>
          <div>  <span class="warn">[INFERRED_ROUTE]</span> <span class="meta">openapi-shelf/notif-svc-v3.yaml</span></div>
          <div>&nbsp;</div>
          <div><span class="hl">→ notif-svc/internal/handlers/payment.go:38</span></div>
          <div>  <span class="meta">router.POST("/notifications/payment-failed", h.OnFail)</span></div>
          <div>  <span class="meta">→ pushes to user_inbox + email_queue</span></div>
          <div>&nbsp;</div>
          <div><span class="ok">claude:</span> The flow is: charge.ts catches the failure → posts to notif-svc…</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">§ Trust grades</div>
        <h2>Every inferred edge carries provenance.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prov-grid">
        <div class="prov-card prov-strong">
          <div class="prov-h mono">tier 1 - strongest</div>
          <div class="prov-tag mono">openapi specs</div>
          <p>Pulled from your <span class="kbd">~/.metalmind/specs/</span> shelf. Routes match exactly; types are checked.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prov-card prov-medium">
          <div class="prov-h mono">tier 2 - medium</div>
          <div class="prov-tag mono">framework callers</div>
          <p>Java RestTemplate, WebClient, Feign clients with annotated routes. Strong enough for navigation; verify before refactor.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prov-card prov-weak">
          <div class="prov-h mono">tier 3 - opt-in</div>
          <div class="prov-tag mono">url literals</div>
          <p>String-literal URL matching as a last resort. Off by default; surfaces with explicit <span class="kbd">INFERRED_URL_LITERAL</span> grade.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <PageCTA heading="Ready to give Claude eyes across every repo?" />
</BaseLayout>
